# SPEC GOLDEN — hand-written from css-flexbox-1 §9.7 (resolve flexible
# lengths) before the code existed, never regenerated.
#
# `flex: 1` is the shorthand for `1 1 0`: grow 1, shrink 1, basis 0. So each
# item's flex base size is 0 cells, not the width of its text — the basis is
# what the item starts from, and the text only matters through the automatic
# minimum size (§4.5), which here is min-content = 1 cell per item and never
# binds.
#
# §9.7 step 1: sum of hypothetical outer main sizes = 0, container inner main
#   size = 80, so 0 < 80 and this is a *grow* pass.
# §9.7 step 2: no item is frozen — every grow factor is 1, and base size
#   equals hypothetical main size.
# §9.7 step 4: remaining free space = 80 - 0 = 80, distributed by grow factor:
#   each item gets 80 * (1/3) = 26.666… cells.
# §9.7 step 5: no min/max violations (1 <= 26 for every item), so all three
#   freeze at once and the loop ends.
#
# Whole cells: 26.666… floors to 26 each, which is 78, leaving 2 cells of
# rounding. They go to the earliest items in main-axis order, so 27 / 27 / 26
# and the sum is exactly 80 — a flex line that grows to fill leaves no hole.
#
# x follows from the sizes: 0, 0 + 27 = 27, 27 + 27 = 54.
# Every item is one line of text, so the line is 1 row tall and so is the
# container.
#
# The whitespace between the three `<div>`s is whitespace-only and generates
# no anonymous item (§4), which is why there are exactly three items.
<html>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
  <body>  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
    <div.row> flex row  x=0 y=0 w=80 h=1
      <div.a>  x=0 y=0 w=27 h=1
        anonymous  x=0 y=0 w=27 h=1
          line  x=0 y=0 w=27 h=1
            #text "a"  x=0 y=0 w=1 h=1
      <div.b>  x=27 y=0 w=27 h=1
        anonymous  x=27 y=0 w=27 h=1
          line  x=27 y=0 w=27 h=1
            #text "b"  x=27 y=0 w=1 h=1
      <div.c>  x=54 y=0 w=26 h=1
        anonymous  x=54 y=0 w=26 h=1
          line  x=54 y=0 w=26 h=1
            #text "c"  x=54 y=0 w=1 h=1
